    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d162-a6-a2-a2">

                <pb facs="0269" n="209" xml:id="pg209"/>

                <head>Mr. Wolff to Mr. Harrington.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Basle.</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-05-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 29. 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir:</hi> On May 22d, I asked the burgomaster
                    for Berry’s letter, kept by the police director and not delivered to me.</p>
                <p>On the 23d, I received an answer that the letter in question was in the hands of
                    the police director, and I was referred to him.</p>
                <p>On May the 25th, I requested the police director for that letter.</p>
                <p>To-day, at 4 o’clock, the letter of Berry was delivered to me; I inclose you
                    herewith the original. By this letter you will see that he claims to be an
                    American citizen, and refers to his naturalization papers.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. L. WOLFF.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d162-a6-a2-a2-a1.xml" xpointer="d162-a6-a2-a2-a1"/>
